{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
There [Am]is a [C]house in [D]New Or[F]leans
You [Am]call the [C]Rising [E7]Sun
It's [Am]been the [C]ruin of [D]many a poor [F]soul
And [Am]me, oh [E7]God, I'm [Am]one
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
If I'd [Am]listened to [C]what mama [D]said[F]
I'd [Am]be at [C]home to[E7]day
Being [Am]so young and [C]foolish, [D]poor [F]girl
I [Am]let a gambler [E7]lead me a[Am]stray
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
My [Am]mother [C]she's a [D]tail[F]or
[Am]Sews those [C]new blue [E7]jeans
My [Am]sweetheart, [C]he's a [D]drunkard, Lord [F]God
He [Am]drinks down in [E7]New Or[Am]leans
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
He [Am]fills his [C]glasses [D]to the [F]brim
[Am]Passes [C]them a[E7]round
The [Am]only [C]pleasure that he [D]gets out of [F]life
Is a-[Am]hoboin' from [E7]town to [Am]town
{end_of_verse}

